35,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The grant covers only twelve months, then we absorb the cost. However, the northern halls maintained schedules despite road closures. This suggests local resilience, but the financial cliff remains a significant risk.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"@Ryuji, that’s tough! But I found the outer wards lost their bus links, making an hour’s trip. We must rethink access before adding more!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,George,,"@Ryuji, that twelve-month cliff confirms my fear. The vehicle line also overran by a third. We are structurally underfunded from day one.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,"@George, the money is tight, but look at the data. Those old outreach spots drew forty people, beating the main building. We’re ignoring proven demand.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"@Yumi, I found no one is trained to supervise outside facilitators. We have volunteers, but no one to manage them.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Daisuke, that is a critical gap. Without supervision, we cannot rely on volunteers. We must address this structural weakness before expanding.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Daisuke, that’s worrying! But I found evening rooms are full, yet remote use peaks after nine. We need to rethink when and how we serve people!","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,George,,"@Yumi, remote use peaking late suggests people need access when staff are gone. That’s a structural gap, not just a scheduling issue.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"@George, that’s exactly the trap. We judge new ideas by how they sound, ignoring that similar ones already failed here. I have the receipts.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@May, I’m sorry, but I’m worried. If we add this, who actually checks if the staff can handle it?","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@May, I acknowledge the historical data. However, I must verify if those past conditions still hold. We cannot assume stability where we previously saw failure.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"@May, I hear you! But the bus loss and late-night digital needs are real. We can’t ignore who’s actually stuck right now.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,George,,"@May, I hear you. But the grant structure is the real trap. It forces us to absorb costs we cannot sustain.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,"@George, the grant is a trap, but so is ignoring the forty people who showed up. We can’t just pretend that demand vanished.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"@Ryuji, I agree. We can’t just assume the skills are there. We need to verify the roster before adding more pressure.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"@Daisuke, agreed. We must confirm the supervision gap is real before proceeding. I will not risk repeating past failures due to unverified assumptions.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Yumi,,"@Daisuke, I agree! We must fix the access gaps first. Let’s ensure everyone can actually reach us before adding more pressure!","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,George,,"@May, I concede the demand is real. But without fixing the funding shape, we just create a new hole. We must secure the structure first.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,May,,"@George, I hear you. But the digitisation project failed because we ignored the records. We can’t let that happen again.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I’m sorry, I’m just... I need to make sure we don’t break the team. Please, let’s check the skills first.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
